<<~ ahu slot=`#/head`>>

! carriage.bag.tends ~ the cid CAS tier: blobs, references, and the holds that outlast the grace

`cas` is a local read over the cleartext `cid/` CAS tier, with no daemon boot: it lists the blobs the CAS dir holds and DERIVES which the disk projection references (a `.tid` or `.meta` under `bags/` or `wikis/` carrying `textCid`, or a `lar:///…/cid/<hash>` `_canonical_uri`), then reports blobs · referenced · unreferenced · pending · bytes, and names the genesis-manifest blobs as protected (the engine and plugins never sweep). The projection reads as-of-last-projection: a pointer with no loci path reads unreferenced HERE while the daemon holds it, so this read never sweeps. `all=true` lists each blob.

`fetch=<cid>` reads ONE cid through the running vessel's fetch door (fleet holders over Socket B). `pin=<cid> [tier=<t>] [holder=<name>]` holds a blob past the grace until released (`held=true` names a held pin that ends with the vessel's life, and refuses `held-pin-no-life` where the store names no life), and `release=<cid>` frees it. `sweep=true [dry-run=true]` sweeps the unreferenced blobs past their grace where the composite stands; dry names them and moves nothing.

<<~/ahu>>

